Has the time come to separate home and away fans at WSL games? | Football |=
 The Guardian


Has the time come to separate home and away fans at WSL games?


With interest in the league rising, some are calling for dedicated away end=
s at stadiums to improve atmosphere


Fans of Chelsea and Arsenal are seen drinking in the stands prior to their =
WSL match last season. Photograph: Alex Broadway/WSL Football/Getty Images


Elizabeth Payne


With interest in the Women=E2=80=99s Super League on the rise and more club=
s playing at their main stadiums, there are questions over whether to separ=
ate supporters into stricter home and away sections, as in the men=E2=80=99=
s game, or to continue with mixed seating and optional away ends.

From the 2023-24 season, new league regulations required clubs to include a=
n away-ticketing policy in their licensing agreements, a move backed by the=
 Football Supporters=E2=80=99 Association (FSA).


