<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It=E2=80=99s tough to say exactly how Koch=
en=E2=80=99s first club run-out away from Bar=C3=A7a is going, as Lyngby pl=
ays in the Danish Superliga =E2=80=93 one of many leagues lacking in robust=
 publicly available data. The club, just promoted from the second division,=
 have won just one of nine games to date, conceding 16 goals from 116 shots=
 for a 0.14 rate that=E2=80=99s joint-worst in the league. These are surely=
 among the lumps both Lyngby and Barcelona are willing to let Kochen take a=
s he gets some needed professional seasoning.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Those numbers might not jump off the page,=
 but Kochen=E2=80=99s profile still makes him a tantalizing prospect for a =
program that has been without an obvious starter in goal since Tim Howard=
=E2=80=99s retirement a decade ago. The Miami-born Kochen is as comfortable=
 on the ball as any prospect in program history, and already got valuable r=
eps as a training-only member of the World Cup squad. Scouting reports from=
 Europe suggest he=E2=80=99s already proactive about stopping crosses, a go=
od sign considering his slim build. It will be fascinating to finally get a=
n up-close look at what Kochen is all about, should Pochettino give him som=
e minutes.</p>
